      "method": "POST",
      "url": "/services/data/v59.0/sobjects/Service_Request__c",
      "body": {
        "Subject__c": "Installation",
        "Serial_Number__c": "SN-88213"
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

The Composite API executes the subrequests in the order listed and, with `"allOrNone": true`, treats them as a single all‑or‑nothing transaction. Because each subrequest is committed in sequence within that transaction, the Asset is already saved (and findable by SerialNumber) when the `Service_Request__c` before‑insert trigger runs. If any subrequest fails—including the trigger's `addError`—the whole transaction is rolled back and none of the records persist.

