The `registerPublishAfterSuccessTransaction` method publishes the `Deal_Won__e` events only after the DML (the opportunity updates) commits successfully. If the save fails, `commitWork()` throws before the after-success publisher runs, so no events are published and the exception propagates to the caller. Because platform events don't need registering as DML SObjectTypes in the unit of work (they're published via the registered publisher, not via `registerDirty`/`registerNew`), `Application` needs no change.

